# Cargo.lock IS tracked. This crate ships a binary ([[bin]] yodel), and
# the current guidance for any repo with a binary is to commit the
# lockfile: it makes CI reproducible (a semver-compatible upstream
# release can no longer turn a green PR red with no local change), makes
# a dependency regression bisectable, and makes `cargo install --locked`
# resolve what was actually reviewed. Library consumers are unaffected --
# cargo ignores a dependency's lockfile.

# Agent-harness configuration: operator-local, never published.
/.curia/
